{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3246","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3246","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3246\",\"parent_revision\":\"fe2f560535f34943267448894d8cfaa22e9246e88c7feb483e659e2e9df764f7\",\"root_revision\":\"fe2f560535f34943267448894d8cfaa22e9246e88c7feb483e659e2e9df764f7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nmulti-perspective-review/SKILL.md's numbered Steps 1-7 (argument parsing, slug derivation, plan creation, dispatch, synthesis, gate logic) are prose that walks the same branching and sequencing that the skill's own Dispatch Flow Mermaid diagram (now at references/dispatch-flow.md, moved there in PR #3245) independently encodes. Both representations currently describe the identical process \u2014 every branch, condition, and terminal outcome in the diagram corresponds to prose already present in Steps 1-7, and every conditional in the prose corresponds to a diamond in the diagram.\\n\\nThis is the same \\\"duplication \u2014 the same meaning in more than one place\\\" failure named in mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents: the two representations must be kept in sync by hand (as PRs #3240, #3241, #3243, and #3245 this session each did, treating the diagram as a \\\"Reference\\\" cross-check against the prose), and the duplication itself inflates the skill's token footprint independent of whether the diagram is inline or disclosed.\\n\\nAgents consume Mermaid as notation, not as a rendered visual \u2014 they parse the diagram's text directly. That means the diagram's value over prose is branching precision and notation density for an agent reader, not visual communication. Given that, keeping a full prose walkthrough of the same branching the diagram already encodes adds no signal an agent needs, at real token cost.\\n\\nThis repo already has a working precedent for the corrected shape: dh:work-backlog-item's routing sections contain only a Mermaid diagram as the authoritative sequencing source, with zero parallel prose re-narrating the same branches \u2014 supplementary prose there covers only what the notation can't carry (exact tool-call signatures, field definitions), not the branching itself.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: The fix is likely to converge Steps 1-7 into supplementary-detail-only prose (exact MCP call signatures, task body/payload shapes, schema field names) anchored to the diagram as the sole authoritative sequencing/branching source \u2014 not to keep both. This is expected to substantially reduce the skill's token footprint on its own, making backlog item #3244's auto-disclosure heuristic a secondary concern for this file specifically (though #3244 remains relevant for process-siren's general behavior across other skills).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 surfaced while reviewing PRs #3240-#3245 against multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"38dc5be12cb442bd17cc985bd58ca878e961366e74dc9a0d9f3c55ec41430f34\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRBa9Cw\"}"}